{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790726872,"nonce":"pA5zYVkxjk6v/LP/t1U7zaO7hiA=","title":"Lazy optimization holds the scratch mutex across the HIR pipeline","message":"install_lazy_compiler keeps Scratches::slots locked while it copies reachable HIR, runs the per-function optimization pipeline, dumps HIR, and extracts the optimized body. The same happens while optimizing an outlined region.\n\nThis serializes a first-call optimizer, warm-up worker, and promotion work even when they are optimizing different functions. It also makes a short scratch registry lock inherit the full latency of lowering and optimization.\n\nPool scratch modules by source module. Take one under the registry lock, release the lock for all HIR work, then return it. The single-worker path reuses one scratch as before; overlapping jobs receive separate scratch modules.","files":null}]}